Revision history for Perl extension Sereal-Merger

6.000_001
  * read protocol v5 and v6 documents: YES/NO booleans, FLOAT_128, zstd
    compression and keyed checksums (checksum_policy, checksum_vN_key)
  * when writing an older protocol version, rewrite YES/NO to TRUE/FALSE
    and CANONICAL_UNDEF to UNDEF, and refuse FLOAT_128
  * fix compressed output, which could not be decoded; add
    compress => SRL_ZLIB and SRL_ZSTD, a compress_level option, and
    export the SRL_* compression constants
  * bounds-check fixed-size payloads; LONG_DOUBLE is sizeof(long double)
  * fix misaligned loads when hashing strings for dedupe_strings
  * fix merging protocol v1 input, which started reading at the magic
    string and copied bytes from past the end of the input
  * check the regexp modifiers tag without its track bit and bounds-check
    it, and check for the end of input after OBJECT
  * fix a heap overflow writing EXTEND items once wider COPY offsets in
    the output had used up the space reserved for the input
  * append_all() reserves output space per document from its length,
    not once from SvLEN of the inputs (0 for hash keys)
  * forget the tracked offsets of earlier documents, so a reference can
    no longer resolve into another (or a failed) document
  * check COPY targets without their track bit, and reject a COPY of a
    COPY, like Sereal::Decoder
  * bump Sereal prereq version to 6.000_001

4.004 Nov 13 2017
  * last release before this file existed
